    {
      "id": 107050,
      "name": "LevelUpLeo",
      "username": "LevelUpLeo",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/levelupleo/{size}/2394_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-07-01T11:15:27.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Reckless\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/48/2467_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Reckless:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think that she has one.&nbsp; I'll have to talk to a friend who just bought all of the Sentinels game (ALL of it, save for out-of-print promo cards).&nbsp; As far as I know he should have one for her.&nbsp; I definitely want all of them, too.&nbsp; I have all of the cards in the game, but I only have the bio cards for Ambuscade and Unity.EDIT:&nbsp; And having those bios on the cards are quite handy for introducing players to these characters.&nbsp; It's much, much easier telling someone \"Here is Unity!&nbsp; This bio card explains her quite well,\" rather than \"Let me ramble on about this character I like.&nbsp; Did I not do a good job?&nbsp; Let me pull out The Internet and make you read it on my phone/laptop/tablet.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Yeah, they've been quite handy for that reason. This is also why I tend to open up my rule book to new players and be like \"pick any hero that might interest you, while keeping the complexity in mind\".</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I'm finding it cool that I noticed something that a lot of people didn't. Like I said, this doesn't affect the game play that much, so I didn't figure anyone else would care about these cards.&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 13,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:37:09.031Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
