      "display_username": "LevelUpLeo",
      "primary_group_name": null,
      "flair_name": null,
      "flair_url": null,
      "flair_bg_color": null,
      "flair_color": null,
      "flair_group_id": null,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"Reckless\"]\n\nI think that she has one.&nbsp; I&#39;ll have to talk to a friend who just bought all of the Sentinels game (ALL of it, save for out-of-print promo cards).&nbsp; As far as I know he should have one for her.&nbsp; I definitely want all of them, too.&nbsp; I have all of the cards in the game, but I only have the bio cards for Ambuscade and Unity.EDIT:&nbsp; And having those bios on the cards are quite handy for introducing players to these characters.&nbsp; It&#39;s much, much easier telling someone &quot;Here is Unity!&nbsp; This bio card explains her quite well,&quot; rather than &quot;Let me ramble on about this character I like.&nbsp; Did I not do a good job?&nbsp; Let me pull out The Internet and make you read it on my phone/laptop/tablet.&quot;\n\n[/quote]\n\n&nbsp;\n\nYeah, they&#39;ve been quite handy for that reason. This is also why I tend to open up my rule book to new players and be like &quot;pick any hero that might interest you, while keeping the complexity in mind&quot;.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nI&#39;m finding it cool that I noticed something that a lot of people didn&#39;t. Like I said, this doesn&#39;t affect the game play that much, so I didn&#39;t figure anyone else would care about these cards.&nbsp;\n",
